# Keep the build context small and cache-stable. Anything listed here either
# gets rebuilt inside the image or must never enter it.

# Rebuilt by `bun install` in the builder stage; a host copy would be the wrong
# arch and would defeat the manifests-first layer cache.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Rebuilt by `bun run build`.
#
# NOTE: do not add a bare `build/` or `**/build/` here. Docker matches those
# patterns against the FILE `bin/build` as well as against directories, which
# silently drops the build script from the context — the image then fails with
# `bin/build: No such file or directory` at `RUN bun run build`, which reads
# like a missing-file bug rather than an ignore-rule bug. Our build output is
# `dist/` anyway; there is no `build/` directory to exclude.
dist/
**/dist/
.vite/

# Never a build input — and .git would carry credentials from a CI checkout.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Local scratch, docs, and editor/agent state: not build inputs.
tmp/
docs/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Secrets. The container gets its config from env at run time, never baked in.
.env
.env.*

# Local database dumps. `pg_dump` output from a dev instance holds every encrypted
# upstream credential; baking one into a published image would be a leak.
*.sql
*.dump
*.dump.gz

# Per-Account CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR trees, if anyone runs the router outside a
# container and leaves them in the repo. These hold LIVE subscription credentials
# in cleartext — not encrypted by ENCRYPTION_KEY — so they must never reach a
# build context, let alone a published image.
.claude-config/
**/.claude-config/

# Test/coverage output.
coverage/
*.log
